Yes, reset the snake position too. A reset should restore every piece of changing game state to its initial value:

- `snake`: starting segments and position
- `direction`: initial direction, for example right
- `food`: generate a new food position
- `score`: `0`
- game-over message: clear it
- game interval: stop the old loop and start a new one

A typical structure is:

```js
const resetGame = () => {
    clearInterval(gameInterval);

    snake = [
        { x: 10, y: 10 },
        { x: 9, y: 10 },
        { x: 8, y: 10 }
    ];

    direction = { x: 1, y: 0 };
    food = generateFood();
    score = 0;
    info.textContent = "";

    drawGame();
    gameInterval = setInterval(gameLoop, 150);
