Use CSS `animation` with `@keyframes` to fade the banner in while it grows slightly. Add this to your existing `#gameOverBanner` styles:

```css
#gameOverBanner {
  animation: banner-pop 250ms ease-out;
}

@keyframes banner-pop {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: scale(0.92);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: scale(1);
  }
}
```

`250ms` sets the duration, and `ease-out` makes the motion settle gently. CSS handles it automatically; you don’t need a library or JavaScript. Keep your `[hidden] { display: none; }` rule so the banner stays hidden until shown.

Optional: respect reduced-motion preferences by disabling the animation for users who request less motion:

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  #gameOverBanner {
    animation: none;
  }
}
```

