Yes. Add `drawGame()` inside the existing `saveModeBtn` click handler, immediately after `setDifficulty(selectedValue)`. No second listener is needed:

```js
setDifficulty(selectedValue);
drawGame();
```

`setDifficulty(...)` updates the game settings; `drawGame()` redraws the canvas using the updated state.

One distinction: if difficulty changes the game speed, redrawing won’t change an interval that’s already running. You can restart it while the game is active:

```js
if (!isPaused && !isGameOver) {
  startGame();
}
```

