In `game.js`, put the variable at module/global scope:

```js
let audioContext = null;

function initializeAudio() {
  if (!audioContext) {
    audioContext = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();
  }

  if (audioContext.state === 'suspended') {
    audioContext.resume();
  }
}
```

The first check creates the context only once; the second resumes it if the browser suspended it. Call `initializeAudio()` inside your **existing Start button click handler**. Browsers generally require a user gesture to start audio, so don’t add another click listener if the handler is already there.

Modern browsers support `new AudioContext()`; the `webkitAudioContext` fallback is optional for older browsers.

